      "writtenOn": "2022-07-07T17:04:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had also noticed the higher `COUNT`, although I don\u0027t know if that would necessarily affect the mV and mW measurements.\n\nFYI, these are the version numbers in my local setup:\n\n```\n$ servod -v\nservod v1.0.1362\n\n$ sudo servo_updater -b servo_micro \n\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d Waiting for USB device \u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\u003d\nCurrent servo_micro version is   servo_micro_v2.4.57-ce329f64f\nAvailable servo_micro version is servo_micro_v2.4.57-ce329f64f\nNo version update needed\n```\n\n\u003e Also, it looks like your board might be running at 2.8V \n\nMy servo micro is connected to a USB-C to USB-A 4 port hub. It\u0027s only powered by the USB-C port of my laptop, but I don\u0027t think that should be a problem in this case. I also connect the JLink to the same hub and it usually worked as expected.\n\nCould this be affected by the switches on the board?",
      "parentUuid": "130955c3_c76abde6",
      "revId": "ba6f7c1597f5eae767f44e11fd0966eea8f04675",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
